          "description": {
            "comment": "The Madagascan rousette (Rousettus madagascariensis) is a species of megabat in the family Pteropodidae endemic to Madagascar. Its natural habitat is subtropical or tropical dry forests (from Wikipedia entry). This sample of a male individual was procured by Cara Brook and Hafaliana Christian Ranaivoson for a longitudinal field study on viral dynamics and to generate a high-quality reference genome for the Vertebrate Genomes Project (VGP). Sequencing and genome assembly were conducted at the Vertebrate Genome Lab (VGL) at the Rockefeller University, led by Erich D. Jarvis, Giulio Formenti, and Jennifer Balacco.",
